<title>USA: Morton Int'l spin-off will be tax-free.</title>
<headline>Morton Int'l spin-off will be tax-free.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morton International Inc said Monday the Internal Revenue Service has determined that the upcoming spin-off of its specialty chemicals and salt businesses will be tax-free to its shareholders.</p>
<p>Morton is also combining its Automotive Safety Products business with Autoliv AB, the Swedish car safety equipment maker. Morton shareholders are scheduled to vote on the proposal at a special meeting scheduled for April 24.</p>
<p>Morton and Autoliv expect the transactions to close by early May.</p>
<p>Morton shares closed up 1/4 Monday at 43.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
